From: Aleksander Pejcic <apejcic@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:30:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(scheduler): concurrent chunked prefill (CP) via --long-prefill-token-threshold (squashed, rebased on v0.5.18)

Squash of the 8-commit concurrent-chunked-prefill stack (previously based on
12a455a910) onto SGLang v0.5.18 (ff4c6e641d):
  - skip every mid-prefill request when streaming, not just the last
  - don't count a parked chunked request as in-flight
  - derive contains_last_prefill_chunk from batch membership
  - pluralize chunked_req to chunked_reqs at capacity 1
  - enable concurrent chunked prefill via --long-prefill-token-threshold
  - cover per-request EAGLE prefill tail-token substitution
  - thread ceiling/capacity/reservation through ignore_eos prefill
  - expose concurrent chunked prefill depth + cap on the unified path

ring-pad backport (agent-patch-33872) intentionally excluded — fixed upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

